course: dictionary
lesson: 11247
title: Worried: a feeling and a past tense
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Worried is a feeling word. When you are worried, you feel unhappy and nervous because you think something bad might happen. «In a hospital or doctor's waiting room you speak quietly and stay seated, because patients may be ill or worried.» The clue is the word ill: patients feel nervous because they might be sick.
explain: Worried can also be a verb. It is the past form of worry, so it tells you what happened earlier. «He worried all night about his sick dog.» Worry, worries, worried and worrying all come from the same word, like walk, walks, walked and walking.
explain: To find out which one you have, try a swap. If "felt nervous" fits, worried is describing a feeling. If the sentence is about something that happened in the past, worried is the verb. You can also say "more worried" or "most worried" to show how strong a feeling is.
fact: Worried means unhappy and nervous because you think something bad might happen.
fact: Worried is also the past form of worry: worry, worries, worried, worrying.
fact: «More worried» and «most worried» show how strong a worry is.
fact: If you are worried about something online or about a person, tell a trusted adult. You will not be in trouble.
fact: Talking to a trusted adult helps, and breathing slowly can calm you when you feel worried.
exercise: «The children were worried about their new school.» What does worried mean here? | *Unhappy and nervous about something that might go wrong | Excited and full of joy | Bright and shiny | Tired after a long walk
exercise: «He worried all night about his sick dog.» What form of worry is worried here? | A noun for a type of dog | *Past form of worry, telling what happened | Adjective, describing a dog
exercise: Copy the past form of worry from this sentence: «Mia worries when her brother is late, but she worried last night too.» | *worried | worrying | worries | worry
test: In the story, Sam frowned and could not sleep. «He was worried about the storm.» How does Sam feel? | Proud of his garden | Hungry for dinner | *Nervous and unhappy | Calm and sleepy
test: Which is the best thing to do if you are worried about someone's safety? | Wait and hope it stops | Keep it secret forever | Post it online for everyone to see | *Tell a trusted adult, who knows who to talk to
exam: Which sentence uses worried as an adjective, describing a feeling? | *The girl looked worried and kept biting her nails | The boys worried about the test last week | The mother worried all evening
